lesson: 228
title: Counting in the classroom
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: When children are put into groups, tables or boats, nobody may be left out: a smaller last group still needs its own table, boat or grown-up.
explain: So divide, and if anything is left over, take one more.
explain: 30 children at tables of 4: 30 ÷ 4 = 7 tables with 2 children left over, so 7 + 1 = 8 tables.
vars: a=name c=17..33 g=4..8
need: c % g != 0
answer: (c - c % g) / g + 1
exercise: {c} children sit at tables of {g}. How many tables are needed so that every child has a seat?
exercise: {c} children go on a class trip. One grown-up must go with every {g} children. How many grown-ups are needed?
exercise: Rowing boats on the lake hold {g} children each. How many boats does a class of {c} children need?
exercise: Each tub of paints is shared by {g} children. How many tubs are needed for {c} children?
exercise: {a}'s class of {c} children is going to the museum by car, {g} children in each car. How many cars are needed?
exercise: {c} kids, tables seat {g}, how many tables we need
exercise: class trip {c+1}, no {c} kids, 1 adult per {g}. how many adults
exercise: {a} says {(c - c % g) / g} tables will do for {c} kids at tables of {g}. enough? how many tables really
exercise: {c} kids, canoes take {g}, how many canoes, and dont forget the life jackets lol
exercise: footy club, {c} of us, minibus takes {g}. how many minibus trips
exercise: How many groups of at most {g} can {c} children make if every child must be in a group and as few groups as possible are used?
test: What is the smallest number of tables seating {g} each that will seat all {c} children in a class?
test: Taxis take {g} children each. What is the least number of taxis that can carry {c} children?
test: {c} pupils want a ride on the little train, and each carriage seats {g}. How many carriages must the train have to take them all at once?
test: {c} of us n a tent sleeps {g}. how many tents
test: we got {c} kids for the party, oh and the cake's chocolate. tables of {g}, how many tables
test: {c} children from {a}'s class go to the zoo with their teacher; one parent helper is needed for every {g} children. How many parent helpers are needed?
exam: Determine the minimum number of tables, each accommodating {g} pupils, required to seat a class of {c.words} pupils in its entirety.
exam: It is given that one adult supervisor is required in respect of every {g} children or part thereof. Ascertain the number of supervisors required for {c} children.
exam: A party of {c} pupils is to be conveyed in vehicles each carrying not more than {g} pupils. State the least number of vehicles required.
exam: Compute the smallest number of boats of capacity {g} sufficient to convey {c} children simultaneously.
exercise: The school has "tightened its belt", so each minibus now takes {g} children and no more. How many minibuses are needed for {c} children?
exercise: {c} kids, tables of {g}, n the "spirited" ones (aka the little terrors) still need a table too, nobody left out. how many tables, think
test: {a}'s teacher is "not in today", so her class joins another and {c} children in all sit at tables of {g}. What is the least number of tables they need?
